1
00:00:00,121 --> 00:00:02,993
In the garden, everything just broke.

2
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:07,596
Two people hiding from the God who made them.

3
00:00:09,026 --> 00:00:10,641
But before He sentenced the guilty...

4
00:00:11,431 --> 00:00:12,262
He made a promise.

5
00:00:13,214 --> 00:00:13,822
To the enemy.

6
00:00:13,822 --> 00:00:15,785
"It shall bruise thy head...

7
00:00:16,552 --> 00:00:19,607
and thou shalt bruise his heel." Centuries

8
00:00:19,668 --> 00:00:20,492
before the cross.

9
00:00:21,621 --> 00:00:22,813
Before the empty tomb...

10
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:25,855
The oldest promise in the Bible is about to

11
00:00:25,875 --> 00:00:26,175
be kept.

12
00:00:27,668 --> 00:00:29,043
The Seed of the Woman.

13
00:00:29,848 --> 00:00:31,718
Something has just gone terribly wrong in the

14
00:00:31,758 --> 00:00:32,060
garden.

15
00:00:33,147 --> 00:00:35,400
The two people God made have believed a lie,

16
00:00:35,863 --> 00:00:38,826
eaten what He forbade, and now for the first

17
00:00:38,866 --> 00:00:41,391
time in the world they are hiding from Him.

18
00:00:41,405 --> 00:00:44,825
"And they heard the voice of the LORD God walking

19
00:00:44,825 --> 00:00:47,794
in the garden in the cool of the day: and Adam

20
00:00:47,915 --> 00:00:50,389
and his wife hid themselves from the presence

21
00:00:50,473 --> 00:00:53,570
of the LORD God amongst the trees of the garden."

22
00:00:54,058 --> 00:00:55,109
And God comes looking.

23
00:00:56,276 --> 00:00:59,672
Not with armies, not yet with judgment with

24
00:00:59,712 --> 00:01:00,234
a question.

25
00:01:01,459 --> 00:01:03,914
"Where art thou?" Then the blame goes around

26
00:01:03,934 --> 00:01:04,396
the circle.

27
00:01:05,282 --> 00:01:07,736
The man blames the woman, and the woman blames

28
00:01:07,776 --> 00:01:11,061
the serpent: "The serpent beguiled me, and

29
00:01:11,242 --> 00:01:14,063
I did eat." Everything good is coming apart

30
00:01:14,124 --> 00:01:14,951
in real time.

31
00:01:15,998 --> 00:01:18,254
This is the moment the rest of the Bible exists

32
00:01:18,254 --> 00:01:21,213
to answer and God's answer begins in the most

33
00:01:21,394 --> 00:01:22,007
unexpected place.

34
00:01:22,260 --> 00:01:24,297
And judgment has to fall.

35
00:01:25,405 --> 00:01:28,161
Eden cannot simply carry on as if nothing happened.

36
00:01:28,925 --> 00:01:32,520
Innocence is gone, death has entered, and the

37
00:01:32,580 --> 00:01:34,975
people made for God's presence are now afraid

38
00:01:35,016 --> 00:01:36,552
of it, crouched in the trees.

39
00:01:37,229 --> 00:01:39,404
But underneath the fear is a deeper trouble.

40
00:01:40,270 --> 00:01:42,563
In trusting the serpent over their Maker, the

41
00:01:42,603 --> 00:01:44,420
man and the woman have taken the creature's

42
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:46,009
word against the Creator's.

43
00:01:47,294 --> 00:01:49,068
And there is no human way back.

44
00:01:50,194 --> 00:01:52,527
You cannot un-eat the fruit, or argue your

45
00:01:52,568 --> 00:01:55,007
way back into the garden, or stop the death

46
00:01:55,128 --> 00:01:56,410
that has now entered the world.

47
00:01:57,818 --> 00:02:00,253
If rescue is going to come, it has to come

48
00:02:00,319 --> 00:02:03,095
from God's side of the breach or it does not

49
00:02:03,095 --> 00:02:03,395
come at all.

50
00:02:04,161 --> 00:02:06,935
Now watch closely, because the key detail is

51
00:02:07,055 --> 00:02:08,696
one the eye slides right over.

52
00:02:08,823 --> 00:02:10,934
When God begins to pronounce the sentence,

53
00:02:11,396 --> 00:02:13,060
He does not turn to Adam first.

54
00:02:13,908 --> 00:02:15,502
He does not turn to Eve first.

55
00:02:16,391 --> 00:02:17,784
He turns to the serpent.

56
00:02:18,370 --> 00:02:21,646
"And the LORD God said unto the serpent, Because

57
00:02:21,726 --> 00:02:24,865
thou hast done this, thou art cursed above

58
00:02:25,106 --> 00:02:28,337
all cattle, and above every beast of the field."

59
00:02:28,858 --> 00:02:29,849
That much is pure curse.

60
00:02:31,024 --> 00:02:33,277
But listen to what God weaves into it next

61
00:02:33,901 --> 00:02:36,501
still speaking to the serpent, still before

62
00:02:36,561 --> 00:02:38,560
He has said a single word of sentence to the

63
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:41,824
man or the woman: "And I will put enmity between

64
00:02:41,864 --> 00:02:44,347
thee and the woman, and between thy seed and

65
00:02:44,448 --> 00:02:48,090
her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou

66
00:02:48,151 --> 00:02:49,446
shalt bruise his heel." Let that land.

67
00:02:51,876 --> 00:02:54,410
Before God says a word to Eve about sorrow,

68
00:02:54,732 --> 00:02:57,390
before a word to Adam about thorns and dust

69
00:02:57,853 --> 00:03:00,834
both of which come after this the first promise

70
00:03:00,874 --> 00:03:03,555
of rescue in the Bible is spoken into the enemy's

71
00:03:03,716 --> 00:03:07,840
own curse: a deliverer is coming who will crush

72
00:03:07,880 --> 00:03:08,180
him.

73
00:03:08,189 --> 00:03:10,205
And the promise is strangely specific.

74
00:03:11,169 --> 00:03:14,507
It speaks of "her seed" the woman's offspring.

75
00:03:15,672 --> 00:03:18,596
That is an unusual way to put it; across the

76
00:03:18,636 --> 00:03:21,001
rest of Scripture a line is most often traced

77
00:03:21,041 --> 00:03:21,729
through fathers.

78
00:03:22,616 --> 00:03:24,611
Here the hope hangs on the woman's seed.

79
00:03:25,877 --> 00:03:29,202
It is a clue, not a proof but it is a clue

80
00:03:29,263 --> 00:03:31,175
that lights up when the New Testament tells

81
00:03:31,243 --> 00:03:32,876
how the Saviour finally came.

82
00:03:32,919 --> 00:03:35,614
"But when the fulness of the time was come,

83
00:03:36,278 --> 00:03:39,759
God sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made

84
00:03:40,020 --> 00:03:41,905
under the law." Made of a woman.

85
00:03:42,954 --> 00:03:45,088
And the angel's word to Mary names what kind

86
00:03:45,108 --> 00:03:49,566
of child she carried: "that holy thing which

87
00:03:49,626 --> 00:03:52,789
shall be born of thee shall be called the Son

88
00:03:52,829 --> 00:03:55,715
of God." Now be honest about what kind of match

89
00:03:55,755 --> 00:03:56,200
this is.

90
00:03:57,496 --> 00:03:59,859
No New Testament writer ever stops, quotes

91
00:03:59,919 --> 00:04:03,074
Genesis 3:15 word for word, and declares it

92
00:04:03,114 --> 00:04:04,644
fulfilled in so many words.

93
00:04:05,634 --> 00:04:08,472
This is not a citation; it is a trajectory

94
00:04:09,252 --> 00:04:11,264
the whole story bending toward one point.

95
00:04:13,022 --> 00:04:15,296
What the New Testament does do is name the

96
00:04:15,356 --> 00:04:15,779
players.

97
00:04:16,650 --> 00:04:17,158
The serpent?

98
00:04:18,365 --> 00:04:21,180
"that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan."

99
00:04:21,662 --> 00:04:22,104
The mission?

100
00:04:22,869 --> 00:04:25,463
"For this purpose the Son of God was manifested,

101
00:04:26,046 --> 00:04:28,826
that he might destroy the works of the devil."

102
00:04:29,348 --> 00:04:30,411
And the crushing itself?

103
00:04:31,640 --> 00:04:34,425
Paul writes to a church: "And the God of peace

104
00:04:34,626 --> 00:04:37,564
shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly."

105
00:04:38,166 --> 00:04:40,594
The opening pages of Scripture planted a promise

106
00:04:41,340 --> 00:04:43,354
and everything that follows leans toward its

107
00:04:43,395 --> 00:04:43,777
keeping.

108
00:04:43,777 --> 00:04:46,657
Now slow down, because a fair-minded skeptic

109
00:04:46,697 --> 00:04:49,166
has real objections here and they deserve a

110
00:04:49,216 --> 00:04:50,846
real answer, not a dodge.

111
00:04:50,955 --> 00:04:54,264
The biggest one: you are simply reading Jesus

112
00:04:54,405 --> 00:04:55,451
into a snake story.

113
00:04:56,638 --> 00:04:59,413
And it is partly fair no verse quotes this

114
00:04:59,493 --> 00:05:02,010
line outright, and the word "seed" can just

115
00:05:02,070 --> 00:05:03,497
mean ordinary descendants.

116
00:05:04,362 --> 00:05:06,245
So we do not rest the case on that one phrase.

117
00:05:07,563 --> 00:05:09,797
We rest it on the shape of the whole canon

118
00:05:10,943 --> 00:05:13,176
the same Scripture whose later writers are

119
00:05:13,196 --> 00:05:16,115
the ones who call that serpent the Devil, who

120
00:05:16,176 --> 00:05:18,915
say the Son came to destroy his works, and

121
00:05:18,955 --> 00:05:21,017
who put a woman's child at the heart of the

122
00:05:21,057 --> 00:05:21,461
rescue.

123
00:05:22,468 --> 00:05:24,641
The thread was not forced onto Genesis from

124
00:05:24,701 --> 00:05:27,565
outside; it was followed out from within.

125
00:05:27,772 --> 00:05:30,290
And what of the line that says Satan is crushed

126
00:05:30,973 --> 00:05:34,377
"under your feet" the church's feet, not one

127
00:05:34,437 --> 00:05:34,838
man's?

128
00:05:36,185 --> 00:05:36,833
Both are true.

129
00:05:37,741 --> 00:05:40,695
The church shares the victory, but only because

130
00:05:40,736 --> 00:05:42,978
it stands on the One who won it first.

131
00:05:44,324 --> 00:05:46,218
You do not have to force any of this.

132
00:05:46,785 --> 00:05:48,958
You only have to follow the line that runs

133
00:05:49,018 --> 00:05:49,610
from Eden to the cross.

134
00:05:50,947 --> 00:05:53,080
And here the promise turns out to cost far

135
00:05:53,160 --> 00:05:54,583
more than it first sounds.

136
00:05:55,730 --> 00:05:58,710
Look again at how the deliverer wins: "it shall

137
00:05:58,770 --> 00:06:02,266
bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his

138
00:06:02,351 --> 00:06:05,347
heel." Two wounds but they are not equal.

139
00:06:06,531 --> 00:06:10,118
The serpent strikes the heel: real, agonizing,

140
00:06:10,721 --> 00:06:12,108
the kind of strike that can kill.

141
00:06:13,256 --> 00:06:16,029
The seed crushes the head: final.

142
00:06:16,340 --> 00:06:17,150
That is the cross.

143
00:06:18,138 --> 00:06:20,693
The strike to the heel is Calvary and it was

144
00:06:20,822 --> 00:06:21,874
no glancing blow.

145
00:06:22,842 --> 00:06:25,216
The Son of God hung there bearing what we had

146
00:06:25,216 --> 00:06:28,558
earned; the death that was our wages fell on

147
00:06:28,638 --> 00:06:28,938
Him.

148
00:06:29,946 --> 00:06:32,339
He stepped into the very judgment we deserved

149
00:06:32,520 --> 00:06:35,959
and took it: "that through death he might destroy

150
00:06:36,039 --> 00:06:39,561
him that had the power of death, that is, the

151
00:06:39,581 --> 00:06:40,927
devil." Do you see the turn?

152
00:06:42,513 --> 00:06:44,364
The blow that looked like the serpent winning

153
00:06:44,747 --> 00:06:47,868
the death of the Son was the blow that crushed

154
00:06:47,908 --> 00:06:48,350
his head.

155
00:06:49,636 --> 00:06:52,451
The victory was won in the cross itself, not

156
00:06:52,612 --> 00:06:56,367
in spite of it: "And having spoiled principalities

157
00:06:56,427 --> 00:06:58,823
and powers, he made a shew of them openly,

158
00:06:59,205 --> 00:07:02,204
triumphing over them in it." And the empty

159
00:07:02,244 --> 00:07:04,679
tomb three days later put it beyond all doubt

160
00:07:05,466 --> 00:07:08,083
the One whose heel was struck rose.

161
00:07:09,349 --> 00:07:11,725
The serpent's head will never lift to win again.

162
00:07:12,671 --> 00:07:15,906
He is a beaten enemy already though his final

163
00:07:16,067 --> 00:07:18,105
end, in God's word, is still coming "shortly":

164
00:07:18,105 --> 00:07:20,788
defeated at the cross, finished forever at

165
00:07:20,829 --> 00:07:21,693
the King's return.

166
00:07:21,998 --> 00:07:24,149
So here is the oldest promise in the world,

167
00:07:25,014 --> 00:07:26,334
and it is still open.

168
00:07:26,504 --> 00:07:27,957
Think about where it was spoken.

169
00:07:29,102 --> 00:07:32,318
Not over an altar, not from a mountain into

170
00:07:32,338 --> 00:07:35,599
a curse, in the hearing of the enemy, while

171
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:38,103
two guilty people stood waiting to be sentenced.

172
00:07:39,389 --> 00:07:42,173
Before there was a temple, a prophet, or a

173
00:07:42,284 --> 00:07:45,805
single drop of sacrificial blood, God had already

174
00:07:45,865 --> 00:07:49,140
named the future: a deliverer who would crush

175
00:07:49,181 --> 00:07:51,945
the serpent and free those he held by sin and

176
00:07:51,986 --> 00:07:52,286
death.

177
00:07:52,268 --> 00:07:54,945
And the serpent still whispers his oldest lie

178
00:07:55,808 --> 00:07:59,048
that God is against you, that your safest move

179
00:07:59,289 --> 00:08:00,811
is to stay hidden in the trees.

180
00:08:02,439 --> 00:08:03,952
But that promise has been kept.

181
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:07,749
The deliverer came; the heel was struck on

182
00:08:07,789 --> 00:08:11,084
a cross; the serpent is a beaten enemy whose

183
00:08:11,265 --> 00:08:13,190
end is now only a matter of time.

184
00:08:13,358 --> 00:08:15,425
So you do not have to climb your own way back

185
00:08:15,485 --> 00:08:16,153
into the garden.

186
00:08:17,481 --> 00:08:20,118
You do not have to get clean first, feel strong,

187
00:08:20,603 --> 00:08:24,182
or be sure your faith is large enough the dying

188
00:08:24,182 --> 00:08:26,742
do not heal themselves, and they were never

189
00:08:26,862 --> 00:08:27,245
asked to.

190
00:08:28,711 --> 00:08:30,883
The promise was spoken in your enemy's hearing,

191
00:08:31,346 --> 00:08:32,129
long before you were ever born.

192
00:08:34,346 --> 00:08:37,831
So step out from behind the trees: the One

193
00:08:37,891 --> 00:08:39,895
whose heel was struck to break the serpent's

194
00:08:39,958 --> 00:08:43,466
hold did not come to sentence you He is the

195
00:08:43,950 --> 00:08:46,495
rescue God named from the very beginning.

196
00:08:47,964 --> 00:08:50,118
Come out, and be found by Him.
